1. Definitions

"Covered Work" means the original RaccoonOS code, configuration,
documentation, artwork, branding, and other material that the RaccoonOS
Project owns and distributes with this license or an express reference to it.
Covered Work does not include Third-Party Material.

"Natural Person" means a human individual acting only in that individual's
personal capacity.

"Personal Use" means use by a Natural Person on devices that individual owns
or personally controls, solely for personal, household, hobby, or
self-educational purposes. Personal Use does not include use:

(a) for trade, business, professional practice, employment, contracting,
commercial advantage, or monetary compensation;
(b) for, at the direction of, on behalf of, or primarily for the benefit of an
Organization; or
(c) to provide a hosted, managed, bureau, training, consulting, or support
service to another person or Organization.

"Organization" means any person other than a Natural Person acting solely in
a personal capacity. It includes a company, corporation, partnership, sole
trader or other business, employer, nonprofit, association, school,
university, research institution, government, government agency,
intergovernmental body, police or law-enforcement body, intelligence service,
armed force, militia, military contractor, and any unit or representative of
those bodies.

"Organizational License" means a separate written agreement signed or
otherwise expressly accepted in writing by the RaccoonOS copyright holder and
the Organization. Payment, downloading, access to source, silence, or use does
not by itself create an Organizational License.

"Third-Party Material" means software, documentation, fonts, protocols,
artwork, or other material owned by someone other than the RaccoonOS Project,
including Debian, the Linux kernel, Firefox, systemd, and their packages and
dependencies.

