Subject to every term of this license, the RaccoonOS Project grants a Natural
Person a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to:

(a) download, install, and run the Covered Work for Personal Use;
(b) make a reasonable number of complete backup copies for Personal Use;
(c) inspect the source form; and
(d) modify the Covered Work solely for that Natural Person's own Personal Use.

No right is granted to sublicense, sell, rent, lease, host, commercially
exploit, or use the Covered Work outside Personal Use.

3. Limited personal sharing

A Natural Person may give an unmodified, complete copy of the Covered Work to
another Natural Person without charge only when this license, copyright
notices, attribution, disclaimers, and Third-Party Material notices remain
intact. The recipient receives rights only under the applicable license and
must independently qualify for Personal Use. Modified copies may not be
distributed without prior written permission.

Sharing a link to an official RaccoonOS download or source page is permitted.
Use of the RaccoonOS name or marks remains subject to section 7.

4. Organizations require a separate license

No Organization receives a right under this license to install, operate,
evaluate in production, deploy, copy, modify, distribute, manage, host, make
available, or otherwise use the Covered Work. A Natural Person may not rely on
the Personal Use grant for activity performed for an Organization.

An Organization must obtain an Organizational License before use. This
requirement expressly includes all business, corporate, government,
law-enforcement, intelligence, military, defense-contractor, militia,
nonprofit, educational, and institutional use, whether commercial or
noncommercial and whether connected to a network or fully offline.

An Organizational License may impose fees, device or user limits, audit and
reporting duties, support terms, territory or purpose limits, and additional
